title: God, Christ & the Holy Ghost – These Three Are One
description: The one true God, the deity of Christ, and the Comforter: who God is, Jesus fully God and fully man, and the work of the Holy Ghost, from the teachings on the Godhead.
output: lessons/doctrine/topic-godhead.html

# One deck for the whole of studies/data/topics/godhead.json, each theme given the same weight.
# Slide text is the author's own sentences, trimmed. The verses the teachings typed out are shown from the KJV.
# Fixed: "come I to condemnation" -> "come into" (1504), "win meekness" -> "in meekness" (12781),
# "the goes willingly" -> "He goes" (1955), "John 8:57" -> John 8:58, shown from the KJV (1471).

=== Introduction
--- God, Christ & the Holy Ghost [title]
overline: Doctrine · The Godhead
heading: These Three Are One
sub: The one true God, the deity of Christ, and the Comforter.
refs: 1 John 5:7; Isaiah 45:5; John 1:1; John 14:26
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from 18028
--- Three that bear record
big: 1 John 5:7 | mark: the Father, the Word, and the Holy Ghost: and these three are one
lead: The Bible does not demand that we figure out the metaphysical mechanics of how three can be one. It simply states the fact of their heavenly record and their absolute unity, leaving no room for human rationalization.
p: It identifies them by their revealed biblical names: Father, Word, and Holy Ghost, and the undeniable fact that these three are one.

# from 18028, 1504
--- Great is the mystery of godliness
big: 1 Timothy 3:16 | mark: great is the mystery of godliness
p: Where the text of scripture presents mystery, the fundamentalist stops, where the philosopher and the theologian continue, pressing on in their vain imagination.
p: Always search the scripture to see if it is so. And if you cannot draw a clear, direct understanding of a doctrine from plain language and context, then it is ok and in fact wise, to leave it to faith and admit your ignorance as fallible, finite man.
callout: Each member of the Godhead has His own will, are their own person, Father, the Son and the Spirit. But these three are one and obey the will of God the Father.

# from 18028
--- The fulness of the Godhead bodily
scripture: Colossians 2:8-9 | mark: For in him dwelleth all the fulness of the Godhead bodily
p: The fulness of the Godhead is stated as a fact, *in* Christ. The scripture does not seek to define His “essence,” substance, or the mechanics of that fulness. God's word simply declares it, its truth, and then warns against the very methods that later generations of men would use to elaborate it.
take: There is no need to explain what we know is true. It is just true.
read: app:doctrine-godhead~18028 | Biblical fundamentalism and the Trinity

=== There is none else
# from 15880
--- I am the Lord, and there is none else
kicker: There is none else
big: Isaiah 45:5-6 | mark: I am the LORD, and there is none else
p: God says He has named Cyrus as deliverer, more than a century off in the future. And just as sure and specific and certain as this prophecy is for Cyrus, so it is for the Messiah.
p: God calls all His shots beforehand, and we see the results are true. And if these things are sure and true, then know the promise of salvation and eternal life in Christ Jesus is as well.

# from 11679, 11678
--- The true and living God
kicker: There is none else
big: Jeremiah 10:10 | mark: the LORD is the true God, he is the living God
p: The Lord is consistently pointing out the vanity, the utter uselessness of false gods. How foolish it is to bow and serve dead things as gods, that cannot save anyone. They are an invention of man's own vain imagination.
p: We worship the living God, through Whom all things were made. The heathen in their fear worship the sun, the moon, the stars. Idols made of wood and stone and molten metals.

# from 8888, 8912
--- God is love, and God is holy
kicker: There is none else
lead: The Bible says God is love. In no uncertain terms He is love.
p: God so loved the world He gave His only begotten Son, Who so loved us that He gave His life for us. While we were yet sinners, He died for us. And because God loves His children, He hates that which is against us. His is a perfect hatred.
p: The Lord is separate from sin. Singular in His perfect ways. Where *we can* love, He *is* love. Where we are called *to be* holy, He *is* holy.
refs: 1 John 4:8-10; Isaiah 6:3; 1 Peter 1:16

# from 8933
--- Righteous, faithful and just
kicker: There is none else
big: Deuteronomy 32:4 | mark: a God of truth and without iniquity, just and right is he
p: God is love. God is holy. God is righteous in all His ways. Faithful. True. God is just. God is not a respecter of persons. He shows no favor or bias.
panel: Mercy | the withholding of what we deserve; Hell and death.
panel: Grace | being given that which we don't deserve; Heaven and eternal life.
refs: Numbers 23:19; Lamentations 3:22-23; Psalm 145:17

# from 10409, 17730
--- Jealous is His name
kicker: There is none else
scripture: Exodus 34:6-7 | mark: merciful and gracious, longsuffering, and abundant in goodness and truth
p: We learn a name for God and it is Jealous. Jealousy is not envy or covetousness. It is fiercely protecting that which one owns. God is saying in this covenant He owns them, they are His people.
p: There is no other rock than the Lord. There is no other name given but Jesus.
refs: Exodus 34:14; Psalm 18:31
