read: app:doctrine-godhead~8912 | The Nature of God: God Is Holy
read: app:doctrine-godhead~8933 | Righteous, Faithful and Just
read: app:doctrine-godhead~10409 | Merciful and gracious, and Jealous

=== The deity of Christ
# from 1272
--- In the beginning was the Word
kicker: The deity of Christ
scripture: John 1:1-5 | mark: the Word was God
p: John hits the ground running. No human genealogies. Not the human birth of Christ, but the divine godhead of Jesus.
p: 5 verses that dispel modalism, oneness heresy. Dispel the “Jesus didn't exist until he was born” heresy. The “Jesus isn't God” heresy. 5 verses that lay a foundation for the faith.

# from 1471
--- I am
kicker: The deity of Christ
lead: In the Gospel of John, Jesus is quoted 7 times making affirmation of who He is, using the divine “*I am*,” as God the Father said to Moses from the burning bush.
xr: John 6:48 | I am that bread of life
xr: John 8:12 | I am the light of the world
xr: John 10:9 | I am the door
xr: John 10:11 | I am the good shepherd
xr: John 11:25 | I am the resurrection, and the life
xr: John 14:6 | I am the way, the truth, and the life
xr: John 15:1 | I am the true vine
big: John 8:58 | mark: Before Abraham was, I am

# from 4882, 6095
--- The image of the invisible God
kicker: The deity of Christ
scripture: Colossians 1:15-17 | mark: the image of the invisible God
p: Jesus is the express image of God the Father, and made through Jesus, all that has been created is His, who was before all things.
p: Jesus forgiving the sins of the man with palsy, and then healing his flesh in opposition to the scribes questioning in their hearts His authority, gives a definitive statement of the divinity of Christ. “Who can forgive sins but God only?” Exactly.
refs: Mark 2:7; Hebrews 1:3

# from 9070, 6365, 17935
--- Son of David and Son of God
kicker: The deity of Christ
lead: It is these two sonships that Jesus was born into. Fully God. Fully man.
p: Being the son of Joseph, even adopted, places Jesus in line for the throne of David, fulfilling the prophets' sayings. The Son of David. But to those called by the Spirit, and given understanding of scripture, the savior of their souls and heir to the Heavenly Kingdom. The Son of God.
big: Mark 12:36-37 | mark: The LORD said to my Lord
p: Jesus asks how can a physical son be called Lord by David, himself a king at the writing of the Psalm.

# from 8503, 9015, 9016, 1791
--- Made a little lower than the angels
kicker: The deity of Christ
big: Hebrews 2:9 | mark: made a little lower than the angels for the suffering of death
p: That the Creator became as the created that he may bring us to glory. And in all things He was like us, tempted of the flesh that He may know our struggles and understand our pain.
p: Jesus, being fully man and fully God, was born as we are. He grew as we do. He waxed in spirit and filled with wisdom, meaning He grew into these things. Jesus as man had to, at every step of His life, choose to do the will of the Father.
p: And so, Jesus wept. And then raised Lazarus from the dead.
refs: Luke 2:52; Hebrews 4:15; John 11:35

# from 9793, 9826
--- He that descended is the same also that ascended
kicker: The deity of Christ
scripture: Ephesians 4:8-10 | mark: he led captivity captive
p: Jesus died for our sins, went to Hell for our sins, and after 3 days and 3 nights, rose again from the dead in triumph. His soul was not left in Hell, neither did His flesh see corruption.
p: In a like manner, Jesus who was captive in Hell for 3 days and 3 nights, rose from the dead, bodily, led captivity captive, as He had victory and took power over death and Hell. He freed mankind from the bonds of death and Hell. He took captive His captors.
refs: Revelation 1:18; Hebrews 2:14-15; Acts 2:31

# from 8302
--- The names of Christ
kicker: The deity of Christ
p: The inspired revelation gives us more names of Jesus, that we may worship Him.
table: Name | Revelation
tr: Faithful Witness | [[Revelation 1:5]]
tr: Alpha and Omega | [[Revelation 1:8]]
tr: Son of God | [[Revelation 2:18]]
tr: He That Hath the Key of David | [[Revelation 3:7]]
tr: Lion of the Tribe of Juda | [[Revelation 5:5]]
tr: King of Kings, Lord of Lords | [[Revelation 17:14]]
tr: The Word of God | [[Revelation 19:13]]
tr: The Bright and Morning Star | [[Revelation 22:16]]
